  §16.5: body_range (4454, 4476)  section_span (4454, 4487)  DIFFER   [L9193 cites it for totality: "every claim supported, cited, or marked open"]
  --- §16.5 body L4454-L4475 ---
   4454 ### 16.5 D3 — totality catches a missing value
   4455     Theorem. If Λ is closed, χ_Λ : ∏Aᵢ → {0,1} is total: membership is decided for every ambient point
   4456     by a finite conjunction of decidable comparisons. Proof. Each bound compares two elements of a
   4457     chain. Λ is a finite intersection of such conditions. ∎
   4458 
   4459  **Verified on every ambient point — all 6,912 of them, χ ∈ {0,1} everywhere, nothing undecided, and
   4460  χ agreeing with membership on every cell.** An earlier pass drew 30,000 uniform samples from a box of
   4461  6,912, which is more draws than cells and still not a proof of totality; the exhaustive test costs
   4462  less than the sampling did. Register 248.
   4463 
   4464  **Worked case.** A species was misidentified — Na II read as neutral neon, and the wrong ionisation limit applied. Every channel had *T* = *I* − *E* ≤ 0 and **every one was refused at entry.**
   4465 
   4466     Totality does not detect that error. It forbids it. The computation never ran.
   4467 
   4468  **Worked case, the other way.** A guard in the author's code returned `None` when an alphabet exceeded a cap, and the caller coerced `None` to `False`. That produced "3 reorderable of 85 trials," which produced "almost never reorderable," which produced a false dismissal of an entire line of evidence.
   4469 
   4470     One silent discard propagated through three conclusions, none of which looked wrong,
   4471     because the arithmetic was consistent throughout.
   4472 
   4473  ⅅ ≥ 1 cannot catch that. Every relation checks out on data that was never measured. Only totality
   4474  closes the hole, because undetermined is not in the codomain.
   4475 

  §16.3: body_range (4364, 4384)  section_span (4364, 4412)  DIFFER   [L9201 cites it for D_phys]
  --- §16.3 body L4364-L4383 ---
   4364 ### 16.3 D1 — D_phys catches a wrong value in the data
   4365  Worked case. Two species in this work, Al II and K II, were first computed with Z_eff = 1. Both have
   4366  doubly charged cores.
   4367 
   4368     The bracket held 56 of 56 either way. Containment depends only on monotonicity of T, and Z
   4369     cancels from it entirely.
   4370 
   4371  What failed were the quantities the method does not use. δ̄ came out near 4.9 with a spread of several units — impossible for a Rydberg series, where δ is near-constant. *V* departed from 4ν/3 by a **median of 50%**, where Na I gives 0.2%.
   4372 
   4373  Corrected to *Z*_eff = 2: δ̄ = 1.271 with spread 0.047 over ten members, and *V* to **0.86%** across the fifty cells.
   4374 
   4375     The bracket verifies the data. V verifies the indexing. An index carrying only what its method
   4376     consumes would have passed fifty-six wrong cells.
   4377 
   4378 ![Figure 16.1](figures/figure-16.1.png)
   4379 
   4380  Figure 16.1. The bracket holds fifty-six of fifty-six under either charge, because Z cancels from containment. The defect
   4381  does not: at Z = 1 it spreads over several units, which no Rydberg series can do. The method was blind; a quantity the
   4382  method never uses was not.
   4383 

  §6.3: body_range (1710, 1723)  section_span (1710, 1723)  COINCIDE   [L9285 cites it for the calendar, "E = 7 is the price of keeping January first"]
  --- §6.3 body L1710-L1722 ---
   1710 ### 6.3 The calendar can be repaired, and the repair is instructive
   1711  The calendar fails for one reason: days(m) is not monotone in m, because February has 28. Relabel the
   1712  months in order of length — February, April, June, September, November, January, March, … — and E
   1713  drops to 0. The 365 cells are identical; only the labels move.
   1714 
   1715  **And the repaired calendar is useless.** A calendar whose months run in order of length is self-defining and unusable.
   1716 
   1717  So the trade is explicit, and it has a number:
   1718 
   1719       E(X) = 7 is the price of keeping January first.
   1720 
   1721  Non-closure is not always a fault. It is sometimes a purchase — usability bought with definitional self-sufficiency. What this book supplies is the price tag, not the verdict.
   1722 

