  §31.3.4 body_range (8733, 8795)  section_span (8733, 8795)
  --- §31.3.4 L8733-L8794 ---
   8733 ### 31.3.4 E(X) on a specifiable slice, and 540 predictions
   8734  The 30,108 pairs are a gzipped file this session could not read. But one slice of the catalogue is
   8735  specified exactly in print, and a slice is enough for the operator.
   8736 
   8737  Candelas, de la Ossa, He & Szendroi (Triadophilia, ATMP 12 (2008) 429) state that the KS list's χ = ±6
   8738  points have Hodge numbers (h, h+3) and (h+3, h) for 13 ≤ h ≤ 128, and name the exclusions: h = 102,
   8739  103, 115, 117 and 119–126. That is a complete cell set — 208 cells — and ℛ applies to it.
   8740 
   8741     E(X) = 540. 498 join failures and 498 meet failures of 21,528 pairs.
   8742 
   8743  24.3.4.1 Which is 540 predictions, not a defect
   8744  Chapter 6 reads E(X) > 0 as what a structure admits and lacks. The periodic table admits 36 such
   8745  cells and they are the elements. Here the slice admits 540 and they are Hodge pairs the
   8746  catalogue must contain if the pair set is closed.
   8747 
   8748  The slice cannot contain them, and the reason is geometric. Two parallel lines have no fixed point:
   8749  the join of (h, h+3) and (h+3, h) is (h+3, h+3). So ℛ immediately names the diagonal.
   8750 
   8751   the predictions
   8752   cells                                     540
   8753   distinct χ values                         5 — only 0, ±2, ±4
   8754   on the diagonal, χ = 0                    112, from (13,13) to (131,131)
   8755   h¹¹ + h²¹ range                           26 to 262
   8756 
   8757  The slice was cut at χ = ±6 and the closure predicts inward. It says the set the slice came from fills
   8758  the gap between the two lines — which is where the rest of the Kreuzer–Skarke list lives.
   8759 
   8760  24.3.4.2 The fourth falsification test, run
   8761 
   8762  The file is missing, so the predictions cannot be looked up. They can still be refuted, because
   8763  the literature states where the catalogue's contents lie.
   8764 
   8765   test                                                                     result
   8766   h¹¹ ≥ 1 and h²¹ ≥ 1                                                      540 / 540
   8767   h¹¹ + h²¹ ≤ 502, the published maximum                                   540 / 540
   8768   mirror partner present                                                   540 / 540
   8769   falling where Candelas et al. record "essentially every site occupied"   540 / 540
   8770   falling in the "thinly populated" tip, where a prediction would be       0 / 540
   8771   refuted
   8772   falsified                                                                0
   8773   individually named in print                                              X₁₉,₁₉ (split bicubic), X₂₀,₂₀ (the 24-cell)
   8774 
   8775     Zero falsifications, two named confirmations, and every prediction inside the region
   8776     published as fully populated.
   8777 
   8778  This is weaker than a lookup and it is not nothing. A prediction landing in the sparse tip would have
   8779  been refuted, and none does. The test is against the literature's characterisation of the file
   8780  rather than against the file.
   8781 
   8782  24.3.4.3 And the void reads the same way
   8783 
   8784                                                                                     cells        predictions
   8785   all h from 13 to 128                                                              232          589
   8786   with the documented exclusions                                                    208          540
   8787 
   8788  The 24 excluded values — 102, 103, 115, 117 and the run 119–126 — reduce the predictions by
   8789  49. The gaps in the published list are not noise with respect to closure: removing them moves the set
   8790  toward its own normal form, which is what §10 says a void should do when it is structural rather than
   8791  accidental.
   8792 
   8793  What remains of item D is the lookup. 540 named cells, a file, and an afternoon.
   8794 
